        "original_id": "a1ef5fa9-f27f-5610-9ce2-7777e2af6190",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lowell George, Ian Hunter, Christopher Cross\n- Bands: Little Feat, Mott the Hoople\n- Songs: \"Ride Like the Wind\"\n\nFacts:\n- Lowell Thomas George was born on April 13, 1945, and died on June 29, 1979.\n- Ian Hunter Patterson was born on 3 June 1939 and is known professionally as Ian Hunter.\n- Lowell George was an American songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and record producer.\n- Lowell George was the primary guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter for the rock band Little Feat.\n- Ian Hunter is a British singer-songwriter best known as the lead singer of the English rock band Mott the Hoople.\n- Ian Hunter was the lead singer of Mott the Hoople from the band's inception in 1969 to its dissolution in 1974, and again for its reunions in 2009 and 2013.\n- On the inner sleeve of the song \"Ride Like the Wind,\" Christopher Cross dedicated the song to Lowell George, formerly of Little Feat, after George died in 1979.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
